  "request": "Which classes inherit from ApiModel (auto_ontology/server/models.py) only indirectly, i.e. through at least one intermediate class of this repository, and do not name ApiModel directly in their class statement? An import alias of ApiModel (auto_ontology/server/responses.py imports it as _Payload) counts as naming ApiModel directly, and a subscripted base such as ListResponse[T] counts as its class. For each, give the class symbol ID and the length of the shortest inheritance chain to ApiModel (2 when the parent class directly subclasses ApiModel).\n\nRequested output columns: class_symbol_id (string), depth (integer).",
  "explanation": "Finds the ApiModel class symbol, then computes the shortest inheritance distance from every class that reaches it through class_bases edges. Classes that name ApiModel directly (depth 1) are excluded, so only indirect descendants remain, with depth 2 meaning the parent directly subclasses ApiModel.",
  "sql": "WITH RECURSIVE target AS (\n  SELECT symbol_id FROM code.symbols\n  WHERE file_id = 'auto_ontology/server/models.py' AND name = 'ApiModel' AND kind = 'class'\n),\ndirect AS (\n  SELECT cb.class_symbol_id\n  FROM code.class_bases cb\n  JOIN target t ON cb.base_symbol_id = t.symbol_id\n),\nanc(symbol_id, depth) AS (\n  SELECT class_symbol_id, 1 FROM direct\n  UNION\n  SELECT cb.class_symbol_id, a.depth + 1\n  FROM code.class_bases cb\n  JOIN anc a ON cb.base_symbol_id = a.symbol_id\n  WHERE cb.class_symbol_id NOT IN (SELECT class_symbol_id FROM direct)\n)\nSELECT symbol_id AS class_symbol_id, MIN(depth) AS depth\nFROM anc\nGROUP BY symbol_id\nORDER BY depth, class_symbol_id",
